@@ -7,6 +7,34 @@ Semantic Versioning.
 
 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Added
+
+- Add `client.Files.Upload` to the v1 client. It takes a file name and a
+  reader and encodes the `multipart/form-data` body itself, so callers no
+  longer have to build one by hand. `WithFileDealID`, `WithFilePersonID`,
+  `WithFileOrganizationID`, `WithFileProductID`, `WithFileActivityID`,
+  `WithFileProjectID` and `WithFileLeadID` set the association fields, and
+  `WithFileFormValues` passes through fields the typed options do not cover.
+
+### Fixed
+
+- Retries now resend request bodies supplied as a plain `io.Reader` when the
+  reader can seek, for example a file opened with `os.Open`. Previously
+  `http.Request.GetBody` was left nil for such bodies and the retry transport
+  refused to replay them, so `Files.Add`, `Files.Update`, `Persons.AddPicture`
+  and `Raw.Do` uploads failed on the first 429 or 5xx while every other call
+  retried. A body that genuinely cannot be rewound, such as an `io.Pipe`, is
+  still sent once rather than replayed truncated.
+- Requests with a seekable body now send an accurate `Content-Length` instead
+  of falling back to chunked transfer encoding.
+
+### Changed
+
+- `Raw.Do` no longer closes a caller-supplied request body. These methods take
+  an `io.Reader`, so closing it stays the caller's responsibility; previously
+  an `*os.File` passed to `Files.Add` was closed by the transport once the
+  request had been sent.
+
