--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -176,11 +176,48 @@ deal, err := client.Deals.Get(
 )
 ```
 
+A retry can only resend a request body the SDK is able to rewind. In-memory
+bodies (JSON payloads, encoded forms) and any reader implementing `io.Seeker`,
+such as an `*os.File` from `os.Open`, are replayed. A body that cannot be
+rewound — an `io.Pipe`, an `io.MultiReader` over a stream — is sent once, and
+the 429 or 5xx is returned to the caller. Readers you pass in are never closed
+by the SDK.
+
 Response bodies are capped at 64 MiB by default. Override globally with
 `Config.MaxResponseSize`, per request with `WithResponseSizeLimit` or
 `WithNoResponseSizeLimit`, and use `client.Files.DownloadTo` to stream large
 v1 file downloads.
 
+## File uploads
+
+`client.Files.Upload` (v1) encodes the `multipart/form-data` body for you, so
+uploads take a file name and a reader:
+
+```go
+f, err := os.Open("contract.pdf")
+if err != nil {
+	log.Fatal(err)
+}
+defer f.Close()
+
+file, err := client.Files.Upload(
+	context.Background(),
+	"contract.pdf",
+	f,
+	v1.WithFileDealID(v1.DealID(42)),
+)
+```
+
+Associate the file with a record using `WithFileDealID`, `WithFilePersonID`,
+`WithFileOrganizationID`, `WithFileProductID`, `WithFileActivityID`,
+`WithFileProjectID` and `WithFileLeadID`; `WithFileFormValues` passes through
+any field the typed options do not cover.
+
+`Upload` buffers the encoded body, which is what makes a rate-limited upload
+retryable. Use `client.Files.Add` when you want to encode and stream the body
+yourself — it accepts a pre-encoded body plus its Content-Type, and follows the
+replay rules described under retries above.
+
